      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That redness and warmth are classic signs of a muscle tear or compartment syndrome, not just simple inflammation, so you should absolutely avoid high-dose ibuprofen which can mask symptoms and worsen internal bleeding. Instead, immediately apply ice packs for 20 minutes every hour and elevate your leg above your heart to reduce swelling. If the pain doesn't subside within 24 hours or if you feel numbness, you need to see a doctor right away, but for now, rest and ice are your best bets.",
      "source": "target",
